  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Keelo
    
    A deep-vein miner working the eastern tunnels beneath Sleek☽ Caemomot, the Nightshelf trading post. Keelo is attested solely through the circumstances of her death during the Ofundis∴flux — a catastrophic event in which aurora-fire fused with volcanic heat and flooded the eastern mining passages.
    
    Accounts agree on the sequence. Keelo felt the flux as vibration before the ice fractured — a detail consistent with deep-vein miners' documented sensitivity to pressure shifts. Temperatures in the passage spiked from approximately four degrees to thirty in moments. She carried her apprentice, ☽'viat, through crystallizing tunnels to the surface entrance, sustaining burns to her flippers and shoulders.
    
    Fourteen miners remained below. Keelo descended back into the aurora-fire.
    
    At the convergence point where the fissures met, she reportedly reached for the concentrated heat — attempting, by all accounts, to contain or carry it. The energy crystallized around her. The rock sealed. Rescue crews arrived three days later — I note the interval — and recovered no body. What they found was a shard of anomalous density embedded in the new crystal face: the artifact subsequently catalogued as **Crypt-seal☽ Teneecloris~**.
    
    The shard's properties are better documented than the miner herself. It produces a faint audible tone. Those who hold it report waking with Keelo's name, and the chronicle account from ☽'eocmoum's trading stall — where the shard surfaced via the Icebound Exchange — describes frost spirals that replicate a reaching gesture, and a compulsion drawing holders toward heat. During the Ritus∴um ceremony, the shard reportedly exploited the ritual structure itself to call the living toward the dead.
    
    Keelo's name survives because the crystal will not stop repeating it. Whether that constitutes remembrance or something else, the ice does not say.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
